{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal","id":411944,"title":"Exalted 3rd ed. Sidereal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-19T13:01:54-08:00","id":411944,"title":"Exalted 3rd ed. Sidereal","content":"Ok in previous editions Sidereal were always swamped with protocol and paperwork. My Question is will this be the same in 3rd edition, where Sidereal can use protocol and paperwork to hinder other Sidereal and Gods. If so will there be some clear mechanics for this and maybe even some charms for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:05:09-08:00","id":411969,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should post it in the &quot;ask the devs 1 question&quot; thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:07:08-08:00","id":411976,"title":"","content":"No. I don't remember where, but I remember dev/writer/editor comments about how the Celestial Bureaucracy won't be working against Sidereals anymore, and how Sidereals have better things to do than filling out paperwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:15:52-08:00","id":411988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=411976#post411976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I don't remember where, but I remember dev/writer/editor comments about how the Celestial Bureaucracy won't be working against Sidereals anymore, and how Sidereals have better things to do than filling out paperwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right, for the most part. The Celestial Bureaucracy may still at times work against Sidereals in EX3, but that'd be a matter of how corrupt it is, not because they hate Sidereals for being Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sids are going to be restored to their awesome position of beneficiary service, where they are respected by the gods. However, we love the corrupt, dangerous side of Yu-Shan so we are playing that up.<br /> <br /> Dealing with fate and destiny is not going to be quite so esoteric as people imagine, but it will be there.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals have a new central antagonist to strengthen their thesis.<br /> <br /> I have conceived of a very intriguing addition to their power set, but I am unwilling to detail it at this early a date.</div> </div> </div> </div>He also gave the impression that younger Sidereals -- i.e. assumed PCs -- will generally spend more of their time acting in Creation than drowning in meetings and paperwork.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: Starglyte</b><br /> It was implied in previous editions that younger Sidereals spent their time in Creation doing grunt work while the elder Sidereals mostly stayed in Heaven doing paperwork. Will this stay true in 3E?<br /> <br /> <b>A: John M\u00f8rke</b><br /> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:17:57-08:00","id":411989,"title":"","content":"That's cool, I hope &quot;grunt work&quot; is made more epic than some of the stupid &quot;make sure this farmer's axle breaks so long chain of events happens&quot; bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:27:45-08:00","id":412157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=411989#post411989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool, I hope &quot;grunt work&quot; is made more epic than some of the stupid &quot;make sure this farmer's axle breaks so long chain of events happens&quot; bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably room for big obvious missions like &quot;These undead are going to disrupt this battle that SHOULD go in Chiaroscuro's favor. Destroy them before they reach the battle&quot;, but I like a well-executed &quot;For Want Of A Nail&quot; type missions. Like, one I had in mind...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are to infiltrate the study of Thousand Remedies, a medical genius. At ten minutes before midnight, he will leave his study to fetch some tea. In that time, slip this included form on top of his work pile, some place where it will catch his eye. Remain nearby for the next three days to ensure his research goes smoothly, and then return to Yu Shan. </div> </div> </div>Said form is a forged document noting that in known smallpox outbreaks, people who worked with cattle were largely immune to the disease, spurring Thousand Remedies in the right direction, thus helping bring an End to Smallpox in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:42:09-08:00","id":412163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=411989#post411989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool, I hope &quot;grunt work&quot; is made more epic than some of the stupid &quot;make sure this farmer's axle breaks so long chain of events happens&quot; bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that any Sidereal who acts like he is too good for that kind of mission is going to find themselves assigned to a lot of them by his elders until they get some humility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:49:06-08:00","id":412166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412157#post412157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said form is a forged document noting that in known smallpox outbreaks, people who worked with cattle were largely immune to the disease, spurring Thousand Remedies in the right direction, thus helping bring an End to Smallpox in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea, though I'd think some disease gods would not be too pleased with such a development, possibly resulting in the Sids having to beat some ass to protect him.<br /> <br /> But seriously, this is a much, much better idea than the things the book suggests, especially the &quot;snap baby's neck in its crib&quot; mission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412163#post412163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that any Sidereal who acts like he is too good for that kind of mission is going to find themselves assigned to a lot of them by his elders until they get some humility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah because <i>that's</i> a good narrative to put front and center for an Exalt splat. Totally. Seriously, just because you're <i>bureaucrat</i>-ninjas doesn't mean missions should constantly default to that kind of mundane-level plot. You're <i>Exalted</i>, for fuck's sake.<br /> <br /> And bringing IC punishment in as a justification for pushing boring OOC splat narratives is unconscionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:58:23-08:00","id":412173,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between not doing it at all IC and rarely (if ever) having it be one of the things that happens 'on screen' at your table instead of it being one of the off screen things that happen during down time. If your ST insists on making it something you have to do a lot on screen then you need a new ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:12:21-08:00","id":412181,"title":"","content":"Look, I just have trouble suspending disbelief that the overworked Bureau of Destiny would assign one of its most rare and precious resources to that kind of drudgery, even during downtime. There are 99* Sidereals (and fewer than that active at any given time, what with being killed by Lunars and all paired with the length of time it takes a particular Sidereal to come into their power - assuming the Fateful Exaltation still attaches at birth, you're still looking at over a decade per new agent before they actually Exalt) dealing with problems all over a gigantic and crumbling world; there really <i>should</i> be other assets the Bureau can call upon for truly plebeian tasks.<br /> <br /> *I seriously doubt Rakan Thulio is still doing his duties, what with being a rogue agent and all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:25:34-08:00","id":412194,"title":"","content":"Just because something seems small and mundane doesn't mean it can't be vital to fate running right and therefore not something they can just outsource to a random spirit of broken wagon axles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:41:51-08:00","id":412203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412194#post412194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because something seems small and mundane doesn't mean it can't be vital to fate running right and therefore not something they can just outsource to a random spirit of broken wagon axles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it might not be important.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that &quot;Mission 1: your Circle of PCs need to annihilate the Yozi cult that is taking over the Nexus docks&quot; being followed by &quot;Mission 2: your Circle of PCs need to break wagon axle so the feast is fish instead of pig's feet so the prince chokes on the fish bone so the peace marriage between him and his father's rival's daughter doesn't go through&quot; is incredibly narratively jarring.<br /> <br /> Is that an important goal? I mean, maybe, sure, if peace is Bad For Fate for some reason, or if the whole arrangement was made by Anathema and that needs to be nipped in the bud before he presides over the marriage and thereby binds both kingdoms to his service for ending their long feud.<br /> <br /> Is it the kind of job that 3-5 Sidereals should be put toward? Probably not, unless the ST pulls out the stops to make it worth the attention of such significant assets (the above case being a possible example).<br /> <br /> Are there ways to do this? I'm sure, but at that point how much are you just making the mission bigger for its own sake, rather than admitting maybe it's too small to devote Sids to in the first place? Assuming no weird interference, etc? Why is this a Thing that's problematic for the Loom, or if it is a problem, to justify such massive resources put on it?<br /> <br /> Now this last bit - the importance will vary from plot to plot, of course, but sometimes it really does feel like an ST would need to invent convoluted plot twists to make these boring missions matter enough, otherwise the result is you just remind Sids that they're bureaucrats and sometimes bureaucrats get shitty pissant assignments. But is that a good theme for an Exalt splat? Personally, I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:35:38-08:00","id":412236,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mission 3: There's a river in the Great Forks region flowing the wrong way. We suspect a Raksha may be involved, go find the problem and kung-fu it in the face.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:42:20-08:00","id":412298,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mission 4: We think somebody has hacked the assignment system. Find out who they are and never mind, everything is fine. Instead come murder the assignment dispatchers. We've been doing many evil things which merit destruction. Thanks!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T21:03:58-08:00","id":412406,"title":"","content":"This seems relevant to the current discussion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephenls</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the topic of Sidereals, it should be obvious to anyone who's ever spent much time working within an entrenched bureaucracy that most of a bureaucrat's time is consumed by what could be called &quot;Time-consuming bullshit.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of which exists for a reason, by the way. If someone takes a sick day and someone else doesn't have a clear idea of who's next in line to process pay stubs that day, shit's going <i>down</i>.<br /> <br /> A lot of Sidereal energy is taken up by time-consuming bullshit that, despite feeling like bullshit, needs to happen for stuff to keep working.<br /> <br /> But a lot of our players haven't spent much time working within an entrenched bureaucracy, and it's not really obvious why managing things to do with nations like Chaya is going to consume so much of the Sidereal timetable that it'll interfere with their ability to pull off kickass ninja ambushes. Nevertheless, it does.<br /> <br /> We're adding more obviously interesting and engaging sources of time-consuming bullshit for Sidereals to deal with, so that it's more obvious why the death squads aren't working as fast as Chejop sometimes wishes (while sighing wearily, making a note, and grabbing the next form from his in tray).</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly think that you need variety in Sidereal missions. If every mission they go on is SUPER IMPORTANT FATE OF THE ENTIRE WORLD HANGS IN THE BALANCE AND YOU ARE THE ONLY ONE WHO CAN SAVE IT, it becomes boring and routine. While I'm all for using Sidereals to explore the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMv0abh4Vrc\" target=\"_blank\">banality of saving the world when it's your job</a>, that shouldn't be the only thing they have going for them. They should be able to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4UVbAgZbUc\" target=\"_blank\">rest for ten minutes</a> without having to worry about cleaning up the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412166#post412166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously, this is a much, much better idea than the things the book suggests, especially the &quot;snap baby's neck in its crib&quot; mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kejak: You're a loose cannon, Shepherd. A soulbreaker orb waiting to go off. I have half a mind to bust you down to baby killing detail for the next two centuries.<br /> Shepherd of the North Star: Sir, I don't...<br /> Kejak: <i>Arguing with me?</i> That's IT! <i>GIVE ME YOUR BADGE!</i><br /> Shepherd: What? I...<br /> Kejak: <i>YOUR BADGE, DAMNIT!</i> You're suspended! Indefinitely!<br /> Holok: Hey, hey, hey! Go cool off!<br /> Kejak: *mumbling*<br /> Holok: *Ahem* So, in conclusion, we're very impressed with your work and will be promoting you to co-Chair of the Convention of Air. This will of course come with a commiserate pay raise and increased ability to requisition departmental resources.<br /> Shepherd: Sir, why does he do that <i>every year</i>?<br /> Holok: I have not a clue, just indulge him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T22:15:07-08:00","id":412429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412406#post412406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems relevant to the current discussion</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty reassuring actually. And I'll admit maybe part of my distaste is being a person who has worked extensively in bureaucracies, and not really liking my art and games to mimic life in that regard.<br /> <br /> More options are always good. Options which feel both epic and kind of...time-consuming-bullshitty are also appreciated, because the current crop of examples of time-consuming bullshit are truly dreadful, imo. Right now it feels very much like Sidereals skew between 0 and 10 pretty quickly on the &quot;mission importance&quot; chart, and I guess I'd rather have the low end shored up so that even the most 'banal&quot; mission is still at least a 4 on the &quot;cosmic import&quot; scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T03:45:52-08:00","id":412594,"title":"","content":"I could get on board with a few mundane missions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mission 5: Ensure that the Dancing Boar's entire supply of scotch disappears.&quot;<br /> *Glug glug*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:06:30-08:00","id":412808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412166#post412166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very cool idea, though I'd think some disease gods would not be too pleased with such a development, possibly resulting in the Sids having to beat some ass to protect him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes things more awesome, though, does it not? In my mind (and in my games!) this is how conflicts within the Celestial Bureaucracy should play out, with a combination of cutthroat office politics in Yu-Shan and &quot;controlling the facts on the ground&quot; in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But seriously, this is a much, much better idea than the things the book suggests, especially the &quot;snap baby's neck in its crib&quot; mission. </div> </div> </div>That actually seems like at least some Sidereal elders and/or sifus are going to make new Sidereals do, not because it's an important mission that requires a Sidereal, but in order to bind them tightly to the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Charlie Stross wrote a novella once, called &quot;Palimpset,&quot; which featured a kind of time-ninja society, and their organization had an explicit indoctrination method, that in fact exists in the real world, called &quot;bonding through shared atrocity.&quot; Basically, they made all of their new recruits murder their own grandparents, and then they made them murder <i>their own past selves</i>. Once you've crossed that Rubicon, you're a lot less likely to walk away, and you're tied very tightly to your co-conspirators, who you all know have committed the exact same atrocity. And if you tried to walk away... well, you're a guy who slit the throat of his own grandparents. Who is gonna trust you, you fucking murdering scumbag?<br /> <br /> It really enhances organizational cohesion; you get the same thing in the real world with organized criminal communities who make prospects commit a murder to obtain full membership. So yeah, I can totally see Sidereals making people do this. Just not for the reasons detailed in the splat.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look, I just have trouble suspending disbelief that the overworked Bureau of Destiny would assign one of its most rare and precious resources to that kind of drudgery, even during downtime. </div> </div> </div>A Sidereal would probably have to be, not just a fuckup, but an ongoing enormous discipline problem for that to happen. It wouldn't just happen in a fit of pique; you'd need a Sidereal who was willfully, repeatedly, and flagrantly derelict in their duties in order for the Bureau of Destiny to decide that kind of hardcore remediation was necessary. Said remediation also wouldn't just be drudge work, although that would certainly be part of it on account of that way you're at least getting something productive out of them, it would likely involve drudge work underneath some gods who are really good at reforming hard cases.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it the kind of job that 3-5 Sidereals should be put toward? Probably not, unless the ST pulls out the stops to make it worth the attention of such significant assets (the above case being a possible example). </div> </div> </div>This is something I've always struggled with.<br /> <br /> A circle of 3-5 Sidereals who are all in the same place, doing the same thing, is an enormous commitment of BoD resources. Four Bronze Faction Sidereals all in one place at one time is probably either literally every Bronze member in an entire directional Convention, or merely <i>most</i> Bronze members in an entire Conventional direction with some high-powered ringers diverted from other assignments. It's a little better if this is official business, not faction work, because that lowers the ratios, but that's still an enormous number of Sids. Even if all those people are starting characters, if four Sidereals are being thrown at a problem, that problem is probably a really big problem. Like, &quot;you guys are four-fifths of the <i>entire</i> Convention on Deathlords, except for your boss, who is an Elder who basically camps out in Yu-Shan and serves on four other Conventions&quot; big problem.<br /> <br /> That can make running group games tricky, because you whipsaw between &quot;why is every problem we face a world-shattering one&quot; and &quot;it strains believability we're being allowed to idle this long.&quot; When of course the reason, out of game, is you have four people who all need to sync their schedules and whose PCs all need to remain more or less together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephenls</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're adding more obviously interesting and engaging sources of time-consuming bullshit for Sidereals to deal with, so that it's more obvious why the death squads aren't working as fast as Chejop sometimes wishes (while sighing wearily, making a note, and grabbing the next form from his in tray).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good lord, I remember reading that for the first time and dancing a fucking jig.<br /> <br /> There were loud, long, and bitter arguments back in the day on rpg.net involving people who were entirely adamant in their belief that Sidereals made no sense because &quot;they can just find and murder everyone, endlessly, if you attract any attention at all you should die, see, look at all these resources they have, if I had control of all those resources I could take down all the Solars no problem, Bull of the North should have had his throat slit ages ago, you fail at splat Creation writers, you fail forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, well... no. Both editions haven't made this as clear as they could, but... the Sidereals have day jobs. All that stuff Chejop Kejak does with shadow puppeting the Realm and working hand-in-glove with the Empress and suchly? That, from the formal perspective of the Bureau of Destiny, is his <i>hobby</i>. Stuff he's expected to keep off the books and not allow to interfere with his work. And when he deploys official resources in pursuit of Bronze Faction interests, from another formal perspective, that's a willful act of corruption that really shouldn't be happening. He gets away with it because he's a huge political power player, but he has to do a lot of heavy lifting to make that work. When he dispatches Ahn-Aru to take care of Lilith, he can't just sign the death warrant; he has to cover all the bases. He needs to expend political capital to justify the hit as an official BoD op (which involves lying and then making sure Ayesha Ura can't poke through the lies and get the op cancelled) or he needs to do things like arrange for Ahn-Aru to be on furlough. He has to go work the Immaculate Order to shake loose some more prayers for Jorst, which, again, he has to do off-book, because that's not part of his day job. And he has to do all that while still doing said day job.<br /> <br /> People seemed to have a really hard time getting that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now it feels very much like Sidereals skew between 0 and 10 pretty quickly on the &quot;mission importance&quot; chart, and I guess I'd rather have the low end shored up so that even the most 'banal&quot; mission is still at least a 4 on the &quot;cosmic import&quot; scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, the easiest way to make banal missions work is for them to be part of overall bureaucratic infighting. Sort of like how if you're playing Dragon-Blooded and your House sends you to do something seemingly mundane, it is probably part of the great game of jockeying for power and position, because you're a Dragon-Blooded and unless you're a willful fuckup, you are probably too valuable to waste sweeping floors.<br /> <br /> I once ran a game where my three players spent a month and a half's worth of sessions wondering why their assignments had suddenly gotten so disjointed and trivial. (They were having fun, they were just confused.) And then suddenly one of them went &quot;Wait a minute. I recognize the co-signatory on all of these assignment orders. Didn't he work for that guy we got audited, censured, and demoted?&quot;<br /> <br /> Why yes. Yes he did.<br /> <br /> Things stopped being banal rather fast after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:14:23-08:00","id":412818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412594#post412594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could get on board with a few mundane missions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mission 5: Ensure that the Dancing Boar's entire supply of scotch disappears.&quot;<br /> *Glug glug*</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Let me see that prayer strip...Hey, you wrote this yourself!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Interesting note about Gods respecting Sids more. Between this and the more positive relationship teased between Deathknights and Deathlords, and the more hands-off attitude the Yozis are to have with Infernals, it feels like 3e will almost be a &quot;kinder, gentler&quot; version of Exalted. Were players ever really THAT bothered by PC infrastructure? It never really bugged me, as it was clear that that was all run by the ST, and my groups always had good relationships that way (even when it wasn't me!). The worst one for me was the Sidereals, but only because it was boring...<br /> <br /> Well, it'll be a different tone, that's for sure, and that was one of the main things I asked for in a new edition!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:18:29-08:00","id":412827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412808#post412808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were loud, long, and bitter arguments back in the day on rpg.net involving people who were entirely adamant in their belief that Sidereals made no sense because &quot;they can just find and murder everyone, endlessly, if you attract any attention at all you should die, see, look at all these resources they have, if I had control of all those resources I could take down all the Solars no problem, Bull of the North should have had his throat slit ages ago, you fail at splat Creation writers, you fail forever.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to finish writing that essay about how finding Solars and Lunars on the Loom of Fate is hard. It uses examples on how finding useful information in real world databases is difficult due to the amount of data involved. The loom of fate would be a much larger dataset because it has ALL of creation in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:22:37-08:00","id":412830,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh, I'm not sure whether making those &quot;choking on fishbone&quot; mission more important will cause people to like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:22:54-08:00","id":412831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412827#post412827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to finish writing that essay about how finding Solars and Lunars on the Loom of Fate is hard. It uses examples on how finding useful information in real world databases is difficult due to the amount of data involved. The loom of fate would be a much larger dataset because it has ALL of creation in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, your RL researchers don't have Excellencies, esp ones which outright decrease difficultly and/or literally <b>guarantee</b> success. It's really just a matter of how much Essence they want to burn, which will probably depend on how important they feel the sitch is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:29:59-08:00","id":412835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412831#post412831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course, your RL researchers don't have Excellencies, esp ones which outright decrease difficultly and/or literally <b>guarantee</b> success. It's really just a matter of how much Essence they want to burn, which will probably depend on how important they feel the sitch is...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yes. Excellencies and such make finding stuff in an almost infinite data source possible. If they know the Solar and Lunar exists in the first place, they could blow lots of essence to track them. If they are look for new exalts, well, how often are they going to blow massive amounts of essence to go looking and find nothing? And there is going to be a lot of finding nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:35:59-08:00","id":412839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412835#post412835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, yes. Excellencies and such make finding stuff in an almost infinite data source possible. If they know the Solar and Lunar exists in the first place, they could blow lots of essence to track them. If they are look for new exalts, well, how often are they going to blow massive amounts of essence to go looking and find nothing? And there is going to be a lot of finding nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the thing, difficulty 5 is a herculean effort. A sidereal with 8 dice can forgo his roll and get an automatic 8 successes, and the essence cost isn't even that high.<br /> With a little more effort, that same sidereal can improve his dicepool (tools, favors, artifacts) and +4 dice translates into a total of 12 automatic successes.<br /> <br /> To them, all of reality is just an SQL statement away.<br /> SELECT name, location FROM fate.creation WHERE type IS 'human' AND essence IS 'solar' AND name IS '%Soulshitter%'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:37:46-08:00","id":412841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412818#post412818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were players ever really THAT bothered by PC infrastructure? It never really bugged me, as it was clear that that was all run by the ST, and my groups always had good relationships that way (even when it wasn't me!). The worst one for me was the Sidereals, but only because it was boring...<br /> <br /> Well, it'll be a different tone, that's for sure, and that was one of the main things I asked for in a new edition!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people seem to have a really big problem with behavior-forcing mechanics. I know, 'cause I used to be one of them! My first few games, I houseruled away Limit entirely, for everyone. I was like &quot;fuck that noise.&quot; And that's okay, really. Those are a hard needle to thread.<br /> <br /> Other people don't like it when PC's are presented in a social context that deeply constrains their actions in ways they feel are unproductive or unfun, even if narratively appropriate. See: Abyssals.<br /> <br /> It didn't help that a lot of the older stuff was written into canon as blanket social norms that seemed brutal and unfun to entire Exalt classes. The whole &quot;no God will ever respect a Dragon-Blooded, ever, they respect mortals more than the Terrestrial Exalted&quot; thing comes to mind. That should have been written as &quot;Celestial gods are Celestially biased; they regard the Terrestrial Exalts as d\u00e9class\u00e9 country cousins unless proven otherwise, although some gods recognize that the Dragon-Blooded are if nothing else valuable potential allies and should be treated with respect.&quot; Instead, it wasn't, and what a clusterfuck that was.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:44:47-08:00","id":412844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412818#post412818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were players ever really THAT bothered by PC infrastructure? It never really bugged me, as it was clear that that was all run by the ST, and my groups always had good relationships that way (even when it wasn't me!).</div> </div> </div> </div>The infrastructure as presented in the books is going to be the first impression for many people and Infernals in particular made a really awful and lasting one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:55:00-08:00","id":412854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412831#post412831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, your RL researchers don't have Excellencies, esp ones which outright decrease difficultly and/or literally <b>guarantee</b> success. It's really just a matter of how much Essence they want to burn, which will probably depend on how important they feel the sitch is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting: &quot;Of Things Desired and Feared&quot;, the go-to Sidereal method for divination, had a hard cap on the number of times you could use it.<br /> <br /> For me it was never really &quot;finding things on the Loom is hard&quot; (although it is) it was &quot;Creation is an enormous place, you're outnumbered 6:1 by the other Celestial Exalts, your useful dupes are about to have a civil war, and you all have day jobs and bosses.&quot;<br /> <br /> (And that 6:1 ratio is me being generous; not every Sidereal is Bronze. It's really more like 12:1.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:33:03-08:00","id":412875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412835#post412835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. Excellencies and such make finding stuff in an almost infinite data source possible. If they know the Solar and Lunar exists in the first place, they could blow lots of essence to track them. If they are look for new exalts, well, how often are they going to blow massive amounts of essence to go looking and find nothing? And there is going to be a lot of finding nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question then is more &quot;should it be that easy, even with Charms?&quot; IMO, no. Because even if you're shorthanded in heaven, you have TONS of minions in Creation who would gleefully go forth and die against the Anathema.<br /> <br /> I'd be glad to see the Loom divorced from some concept of being Creation's Cerebro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:34:07-08:00","id":412876,"title":"","content":"Speaking for myself (as someone who likes the Sids and may not be the target audience) Sidereal missions should involve<br /> <br /> - A level of logical sense to the mission : &quot;We want this kingdom here, because we've predicted this great person will arise in it if it does (and will not if it does not), which will mean...&quot; more than &quot;This guy must die. Because Fate... Why are you still in my office?&quot;.<br /> <br /> - A goal to change Creation beyond simply maintaining the status quo: &quot;If we do this, new agricultural methods will be invented and used, the population of the region will grow, the city gods and the people will grow fat on the flow of money, Creation will move forward to a more glorious state&quot;, rather than &quot;There are exactly 200 peasants in this hamlet; predictions show there we may be at risk of there being 500 peasants in this hamlet in 100 years. Rookie, you need to fix this situation. We do not want any change, ever, under any circumstances.&quot;<br /> <br /> This doesn't actually have to be altruistic - it can simply be &quot;This will make the Bureau stronger.&quot; Whatever, maybe your mission is to capture new secret martial arts techniques. It just has to achieve something meaningful in changing the status quo, something new, rather than makework or just perpetuating the status quo ad infinitum. You're part of a functional bureau who achieve things and change the world. You build and create and enable and recover and restore. You're not just maintenance men.<br /> <br /> - A degree of latitude by the Sidereal in the field. The Sidereal gets a broad goal to achieve, and then uses his or her ability to accomplish the goal. The Sidereal does not get a series of micromanaged instructions that have no real input other than &quot;How do I apply my weird Sidereal magic to these ends?&quot;. Comms with your bosses should be hard, and they should be busy, to create a feel where you're not on your cellphone to your mentor all the time and are working off your gut in a situation where intel and your briefings (which really resemble a meeting between the wizards of Middle Earth as much as an intel briefing) haven't prepared you enough for what you face and the actual issues in the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:35:11-08:00","id":412882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412839#post412839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To them, all of reality is just an SQL statement away.<br /> SELECT name, location FROM fate.creation WHERE type IS 'human' AND essence IS 'solar' AND name IS '%Soulshitter%'</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully admit my whole idea was based on there not being an attribute for different types of essence users. Mostly due to the section in the sidereal book that they can't even find their own exalts unless the previous incarnation died at the appointed time.<br /> <br /> Blah. I guess it is possible that Chejop Karjak gets a list of new Non-Sidereal Celestial Exalts on his desk each morning. He just doesn't have the resources anymore to hunt them down as he likes due to Realm Civil War BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-20-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:40:56-08:00","id":412890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412808#post412808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just makes things more awesome, though, does it not? In my mind (and in my games!) this is how conflicts within the Celestial Bureaucracy should play out, with a combination of cutthroat office politics in Yu-Shan and &quot;controlling the facts on the ground&quot; in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does! I just wish all the banal-seeming missions had suggestions of this. Because it comes across like every other Exalt splat is always Doing Important Stuff, and Sids vacillate between 50% Intern-level Bullshit and 50% Endings Special Ops Strike Team.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412808#post412808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've always struggled with.<br /> <br /> A circle of 3-5 Sidereals who are all in the same place, doing the same thing, is an enormous commitment of BoD resources. Four Bronze Faction Sidereals all in one place at one time is probably either literally every Bronze member in an entire directional Convention, or merely <i>most</i> Bronze members in an entire Conventional direction with some high-powered ringers diverted from other assignments. It's a little better if this is official business, not faction work, because that lowers the ratios, but that's still an enormous number of Sids. Even if all those people are starting characters, if four Sidereals are being thrown at a problem, that problem is probably a really big problem. Like, &quot;you guys are four-fifths of the <i>entire</i> Convention on Deathlords, except for your boss, who is an Elder who basically camps out in Yu-Shan and serves on four other Conventions&quot; big problem.<br /> <br /> That can make running group games tricky, because you whipsaw between &quot;why is every problem we face a world-shattering one&quot; and &quot;it strains believability we're being allowed to idle this long.&quot; When of course the reason, out of game, is you have four people who all need to sync their schedules and whose PCs all need to remain more or less together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think it's an inherent problem to having a flat 100 Sids. Sure that emphasizes that they're overworked, but it makes 5 characters always staying together rather implausible without having to jump through some severe narrative hoops. I hope this is addressed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412808#post412808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both editions haven't made this as clear as they could, but... the Sidereals have day jobs. All that stuff Chejop Kejak does with shadow puppeting the Realm and working hand-in-glove with the Empress and suchly? That, from the formal perspective of the Bureau of Destiny, is his <i>hobby</i>. Stuff he's expected to keep off the books and not allow to interfere with his work. And when he deploys official resources in pursuit of Bronze Faction interests, from another formal perspective, that's a willful act of corruption that really shouldn't be happening. He gets away with it because he's a huge political power player, but he has to do a lot of heavy lifting to make that work. When he dispatches Ahn-Aru to take care of Lilith, he can't just sign the death warrant; he has to cover all the bases. He needs to expend political capital to justify the hit as an official BoD op (which involves lying and then making sure Ayesha Ura can't poke through the lies and get the op cancelled) or he needs to do things like arrange for Ahn-Aru to be on furlough. He has to go work the Immaculate Order to shake loose some more prayers for Jorst, which, again, he has to do off-book, because that's not part of his day job. And he has to do all that while still doing said day job.<br /> <br /> People seemed to have a really hard time getting that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think people don't get it for the specific reason that you've outlined: we really have no details about e.g. Kejak's real day job. What does it entail, and rom it, what can we extrapolate about all Sids' day jobs?<br /> <br /> The &quot;hobby,&quot; as you call it (and it's an apt assessment), is front and center and definitely described as more important and more time-consuming than the day job, whatever that may be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412808#post412808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, the easiest way to make banal missions work is for them to be part of overall bureaucratic infighting. Sort of like how if you're playing Dragon-Blooded and your House sends you to do something seemingly mundane, it is probably part of the great game of jockeying for power and position, because you're a Dragon-Blooded and unless you're a willful fuckup, you are probably too valuable to waste sweeping floors.<br /> <br /> I once ran a game where my three players spent a month and a half's worth of sessions wondering why their assignments had suddenly gotten so disjointed and trivial. (They were having fun, they were just confused.) And then suddenly one of them went &quot;Wait a minute. I recognize the co-signatory on all of these assignment orders. Didn't he work for that guy we got audited, censured, and demoted?&quot;<br /> <br /> Why yes. Yes he did.<br /> <br /> Things stopped being banal rather fast after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great idea! Some of this issue I think comes from Arcane Fate, because Sids have a hard time carving out little shady areas of influence in Creation due to it (unlike how IRL bureaucrats work - for example, see the ongoing corruption pogroms in China...yes, some of it is probably pretextual, but a lot of it is Xi Jinxing actually addressing decades of built-up sludge).<br /> <br /> I guess you can do this when wearing a Resplendency, then the issue is always maintaining a continuity when your Respendency burns out to the next version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412876#post412876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking for myself (as someone who likes the Sids and may not be the target audience) Sidereal missions should involve<br /> <br /> - A level of logical sense to the mission : &quot;We want this kingdom here, because we've predicted this great person will arise in it if it does (and will not if it does not), which will mean...&quot; more than &quot;This guy must die. Because Fate... Why are you still in my office?&quot;.<br /> <br /> - A goal to change Creation beyond simply maintaining the status quo: &quot;If we do this, new agricultural methods will be invented and used, the population of the region will grow, the city gods and the people will grow fat on the flow of money, Creation will move forward to a more glorious state&quot;, rather than &quot;There are exactly 200 peasants in this hamlet; predictions show there we may be at risk of there being 500 peasants in this hamlet in 100 years. Rookie, you need to fix this situation. We do not want any change, ever, under any circumstances.&quot;<br /> <br /> This doesn't actually have to be altruistic - it can simply be &quot;This will make the Bureau stronger.&quot; Whatever, maybe your mission is to capture new secret martial arts techniques. It just has to achieve something meaningful in changing the status quo, something new, rather than makework or just perpetuating the status quo ad infinitum. You're part of a functional bureau who achieve things and change the world. You build and create and enable and recover and restore. You're not just maintenance men.<br /> <br /> - A degree of latitude by the Sidereal in the field. The Sidereal gets a broad goal to achieve, and then uses his or her ability to accomplish the goal. The Sidereal does not get a series of micromanaged instructions that have no real input other than &quot;How do I apply my weird Sidereal magic to these ends?&quot;. Comms with your bosses should be hard, and they should be busy, to create a feel where you're not on your cellphone to your mentor all the time and are working off your gut in a situation where intel and your briefings (which really resemble a meeting between the wizards of Middle Earth as much as an intel briefing) haven't prepared you enough for what you face and the actual issues in the field.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS IS AWESOME I WISH I COULD LIKE THIS AS MANY TIMES AS THERE ARE GRAINS OF SAND ON THE BLESSED ISLE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:35:29-08:00","id":412961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412818#post412818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Were players ever really THAT bothered by PC infrastructure? It never really bugged me, as it was clear that that was all run by the ST, and my groups always had good relationships that way (even when it wasn't me!). The worst one for me was the Sidereals, but only because it was boring...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Sidereals in particular is that the 2e presentation of their relationship to Yu-Shan at large was extremely one-note and hostile. It gave the implication that everyone outside the Bureau of Destiny was positively seething with absolute, all-consuming hatred of the Sidereals because of the Usurpation and would gladly execute them en masse if they could only find proof, which of course there was none because those dastardly Sidereals broke the Mask.<br /> <br /> From my own observations, this basically had the effect of making Sid players go into siege mentality. Instead of going out and interacting with Yu-Shan, they would hole up in the Bureau and only engage with Heaven as a whole when absolutely necessary. This basically wastes the entire setting of Yu-Shan for Sids, because who really wants to deal with that kind of shit?<br /> <br /> Interestingly, this was largely from the same book that had the &quot;Dragon-Blooded aren't considered real Exalts&quot; thing Mercushio mentioned, which makes me wonder a bit about the writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/411944-exalted-3rd-ed-sidereal?p=412876#post412876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A degree of latitude by the Sidereal in the field. The Sidereal gets a broad goal to achieve, and then uses his or her ability to accomplish the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this should be encouraged whenever possible. Half the fun of playing a Sidereal is finding inventive solutions and ways to apply your magic that may not be immediatley obvious. I like to think of Sidereals as the Bullshit Exalted; their magic works works best when they're bullshitting the Universe/GM hard, fast and outragerously enough that the Universe believes it. I'm going to put the next bit in spoilers just because it's a character story. And also long.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Okay, so the last game I played, I was a Chosen of Secrets operating out of the Lap. Eventually, the Solars in the group got tired of the Realm government and it's leader, the ever-popular and high approval Sesus Chenow. Up until that point they had been living secretly, but when the battle started by Auspicious Prospects for Secrets* went off and said that The Plan was that it was time the Solars' identities became known.<br /> <br /> I had an NPC Sidereal as a superior in the city, and she was heavily Bronze (I was indie). As such, she had been supporting the Realm's rule, and had take a Dragon-Blooded officer as a lover. He of course was taking place in the battle, and while a compotent fighter was no match for the Solars, the Dawn's army and the Eclipse's Lunar mate. Best he could really hope for was a messy death. The interesting bit is that they had just had a daughter together; she had apparently forgotten (or just never took) her Maiden Tea.<br /> <br /> The problem was, as I mentioned, I was Secrets, and not so good at any sort of talky thing. I could have just sent a message back to the Realm or something, but lacked legitimacy; as far as they were concerned, it would be a random rumor from the satrapies, at least until months later when they realized that the food shipments from the Lap had dried up. What I <i>was</i> good at was Stealth, to extreme munchkin levels even by Exalted standards. It took several rounds of whispering in his ear with Subordiante Inspriation Technique -- he had a family to think of now, there was nothing to be gained by dying pointlessly, he would serve the Realm far more by raising the alarm, there was no shame in fleeing from the overwhelming force of several Anathema -- but I got him to run far enough in advance of the PCs that they never realized he was there.<br /> <br /> So in one fell swoop I managed to fulfill the will of <s>the GM</s> Jupiter, ingraitate myself to my superior by protecting her family (I had previously hidden her daughter at the Immaculate Temple, which the other PCs decided not to destroy because civilians were fleeing there), and take over her position when she was reassigned for bungling the situation so badly (she had, among other things, summoned a Second Circle to try and deal with the PCs and had <i>completely</i> failed to bind it). And the latter ingraitated myself with the other PCs, because I was able to give them &quot;official Sidereal support&quot; of their administration.<br /> <br /> *One of our house rules was a fairly large overhaul to Auspicious Prospects, because of the fact that it didn't actually do anything. Aside from making it one Charm with four 1 XP repurchases instead of five seperate ones, we ruled that the Maiden whom you had the Prospects for could remotely activate it to give the Sidereal an optional goal for the scene, according to their (read: the GM's) Plan. If you failed nothing bad happened, but if you succeeded you dissipated a point of Paradox.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}